                               │
                               ▼
                           Database
The server has:
16 CPU
32 GB RAM
And suppose it can comfortably handle:
2,000 requests/sec
Your business grows.
Traffic becomes:
10,000 requests/sec
You have two choices.
Option A — Make the machine bigger
16 CPU → 64 CPU
32 GB  → 256 GB
This is vertical scaling.
But hardware has limits, and cost rises.
So you choose:
Option B — Add more servers
                  ┌── Java Server A
                  │
Client ───────────┼── Java Server B
                  │
