One more critical question
Suppose:
A → healthy
B → healthy
C → DEAD
Our LB cannot blindly do:
A → request
B → request
C → request ❌
So the LB needs to know:
Which backends are actually capable of serving traffic?
This leads to:
Health checks
For example:
LB
 │
 ├── GET /health → A → 200 ✓
 │
 ├── GET /health → B → 200 ✓
 │
 └── GET /health → C → timeout ✗
Then:
Eligible servers:

A
B
C is removed from the candidate set.
But this raises another fascinating question:
What exactly does "healthy" mean?
Is:
JVM alive
enough?
What if:
JVM       ✓
Tomcat    ✓
Database  ✗
Redis     ✗
Kafka     ✗
Your /health endpoint could still return:
200 OK
while every real business request fails.
So production systems distinguish things such as:
Liveness
Readiness
Startup
Dependency health
We'll go deeply into this later.
